# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the representations"
msgstr "Pagkakatumbas ng mga representasyon"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore vectorizing */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore bilinearity */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore vectorizing */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore bilinearity */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've now discussed three different ways to represent channels in mathematical terms, namely Stinespring representations, Kraus representations, and Choi representations.\n"
"We also have the definition of a channel, which states that a channel is a linear mapping that always transforms density matrices into density matrices, even when the channel is applied to just part of a compound system.\n"
"The remainder of the lesson is devoted to a mathematical proof that the three representations are equivalent and precisely capture the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinalakay na natin ang tatlong magkakaibang paraan ng pagsasalarawan ng mga channel sa matematiko, katulad ng mga Stinespring na representasyon, Kraus na representasyon, at Choi na representasyon.\n"
"Mayroon din tayong kahulugan ng isang channel, na nagsasabing ang isang channel ay isang linear na pagmamapa na laging nagtatransporma ng mga density matrix patungo sa mga density matrix, kahit ilapat lamang ang channel sa isang bahagi ng mas malaking compound na sistema.\n"
"Ang natitirang bahagi ng leksyon ay nakatuon sa matematikong patunay na ang tatlong representasyon ay magkatumbas at tiyak na sumasaklaw sa kahulugan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of the proof {#overview-of-the-proof}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya ng patunay {#overview-of-the-proof}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our goal is to establish the equivalence of a collection of four statements, and we'll begin by writing them down precisely.\n"
"All four statements follow the same conventions that have been used throughout the lesson, namely that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping from square matrices to square matrices, the rows and columns of the input matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ (the input system), and the rows and columns of the output matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (the output system).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang layunin natin ay maitatag ang pagkakatumbas ng koleksyon ng apat na pahayag, at magsisimula tayo sa pagsusulat ng mga ito nang tumpak.\n"
"Sumusunod ang lahat ng apat na pahayag sa parehong mga kombensiyon na ginamit sa buong leksyon, katulad na ang $\\Phi$ ay isang linear na pagmamapa mula sa mga square matrix patungo sa mga square matrix, ang mga hilera at kolumna ng mga input na matrix ay iniugnay sa mga klasikal na estado ng isang sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ (ang input na sistema), at ang mga hilera at kolumna ng mga output na matrix ay iniugnay sa mga klasikal na estado ng isang sistema $\\mathsf{Y}$ (ang output na sistema).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Phi$ is a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$. That is, $\\Phi$ always transforms density matrices to density matrices, even when it acts on one part of a larger compound system.\n"
msgstr "Ang $\\Phi$ ay isang channel mula sa $\\mathsf{X}$ patungo sa $\\mathsf{Y}.$ Ibig sabihin, lagi nitong tinatransporma ang mga density matrix patungo sa mga density matrix, kahit na kumikilos ito sa isang bahagi lamang ng mas malaking compound na sistema.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Choi matrix $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite and satisfies the condition $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr "Ang Choi matrix na $J(\\Phi)$ ay positive semidefinite at nakakatugon sa kondisyon na $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a Kraus representation for $\\Phi$. That is, there exist matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ for which the equation $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ is true for every input $\\rho$, and that satisfy the condition $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr "May Kraus na representasyon para sa $\\Phi$. Ibig sabihin, may mga matrix na $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ kung saan totoo ang ekwasyon na $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ para sa bawat input na $\\rho$, at nakakatugon sa kondisyon na $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi$. That is, there exist systems $\\mathsf{W}$ and $\\mathsf{G}$ for which the pairs $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ have the same number of classical states, along with a unitary matrix $U$ representing a unitary operation from $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ to $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, such that $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr)$.\n"
msgstr "May Stinespring na representasyon para sa $\\Phi$. Ibig sabihin, may mga sistema $\\mathsf{W}$ at $\\mathsf{G}$ kung saan ang mga pares na $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ at $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ ay may parehong bilang ng mga klasikal na estado, kasama ang isang unitary matrix na $U$ na kumakatawan sa isang unitary na operasyon mula sa $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ patungo sa $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, na nagbibigay ng $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way the proof works is that a cycle of implications is proved:\n"
"the first statement in our list implies the second, the second implies the third, the third implies the fourth, and the fourth statement implies the first.\n"
"This establishes that all four statements are equivalent — which is to say that they're either all true or all false for a given choice of $\\Phi$ — because the implications can be followed transitively from any one statement to any other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paraan ng patunay ay ang pagpapatunay ng isang siklo ng mga implikasyon:\n"
"ang unang pahayag sa ating listahan ay nagpapahiwatig ng pangalawa, ang pangalawa ay nagpapahiwatig ng pangatlo, ang pangatlo ay nagpapahiwatig ng pang-apat, at ang pang-apat na pahayag ay nagpapahiwatig ng una.\n"
"Itinatag nito na ang lahat ng apat na pahayag ay magkatumbas — ibig sabihin, lahat ay tama o lahat ay mali para sa isang naibigay na pagpili ng $\\Phi$ — dahil ang mga implikasyon ay maaaring sundan nang transitive mula sa alinmang pahayag patungo sa iba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a common strategy when proving that a collection of statements are equivalent, and a useful trick to use in such a context is to set up the implications in a way that makes them as easy to prove as possible.\n"
"That is the case here — and in fact we've already encountered two of the four implications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay isang karaniwang estratehiya kapag pinapatunayan na ang isang koleksyon ng mga pahayag ay magkatumbas, at isang kapaki-pakinabang na trick na gamitin sa ganitong konteksto ay ang pagsasaayos ng mga implikasyon sa paraang pinakamaayos ang pagpapatunay ng mga ito.\n"
"Ganoon ang kaso dito — at sa katunayan nakatagpo na tayo ng dalawa sa apat na implikasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to Choi matrices {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"
msgstr "Mga channel patungo sa Choi matrix {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Referring to the statements listed above by their numbers, the first implication to be proved is 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"This implication was already discussed in the context of the Choi state of a channel.\n"
"Here we'll summarize the mathematical details.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tumutukoy sa mga pahayag sa itaas ayon sa kanilang mga numero, ang unang implikasyon na dapat patunayan ay ang 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"Napag-usapan na ang implikasyong ito sa konteksto ng Choi state ng isang channel.\n"
"Dito ay ibubuod natin ang mga detalye ng matematika.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume that the classical state set of the input system $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\Sigma$ and let $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert$.\n"
"Consider the situation in which $\\Phi$ is applied to the second of two copies of $\\mathsf{X}$ together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na ang klasikal na set ng estado ng input na sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ ay $\\Sigma$ at hayaan ang $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert$.\n"
"Isaalang-alang ang sitwasyon kung saan ang $\\Phi$ ay inilalapat sa pangalawa sa dalawang kopya ng $\\mathsf{X}$ na magkasama sa estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which, as a density matrix, is given by\n"
msgstr "na, bilang isang density matrix, ay ibinibigay ng\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result can be written as\n"
msgstr "Ang resulta ay maaaring isulat bilang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and by the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel this must be a density matrix.\n"
"Like all density matrices it must be positive semidefinite, and multiplying a positive semidefinite matrix by a positive real number yields another positive semidefinite matrix, and therefore $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"at dahil sa pagpapalagay na ang $\\Phi$ ay isang channel, ito ay dapat na isang density matrix.\n"
"Tulad ng lahat ng density matrix, ito ay dapat na positive semidefinite, at ang pagpaparami ng isang positive semidefinite matrix ng isang positibong tunay na bilang ay nagbubunga ng isa pang positive semidefinite matrix, kaya naman ang $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover, under the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel, it must preserve trace, and therefore\n"
msgstr "Bukod pa rito, sa ilalim ng pagpapalagay na ang $\\Phi$ ay isang channel, kailangan nitong mapanatili ang trace, at samakatuwid\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choi to Kraus representations {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"
msgstr "Mula sa Choi patungo sa Kraus na representasyon {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second implication, again referring to the statements in our list by their numbers, is 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"To be clear, we're ignoring the other statements — and in particular we cannot make the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
"All we have to work with is that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping whose Choi representation satisfies $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ and\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangalawang implikasyon, muli na tumutukoy sa mga pahayag sa ating listahan ayon sa kanilang mga numero, ay ang 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"Para maging malinaw, binabalewala natin ang ibang mga pahayag — at lalo na hindi natin maaaring ipalagay na ang $\\Phi$ ay isang channel.\n"
"Ang mayroon lamang tayong paggawa ay ang $\\Phi$ ay isang linear na pagmamapa na ang Choi na representasyon ay nakakatugon sa $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ at\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This, however, is all we need to conclude that $\\Phi$ has a Kraus representation\n"
msgstr "Ito, gayunpaman, ay sapat na para masabing may Kraus na representasyon ang $\\Phi$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for which the condition\n"
msgstr "kung saan natutugunan ang kondisyon\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied.\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula tayo sa kritikal na pagpapalagay na ang $J(\\Phi)$ ay positive semidefinite, na nangangahulugang maaari itong ipahayag sa anyo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin with the critically important assumption that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite, which means that it is possible to express it in the form\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa napakahalagang assumption na ang $J(\\Phi)$ ay positive semidefinite, na nangangahulugang posible itong ipahayag sa anyong\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some way of choosing the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$.\n"
"In general there will be multiple ways to do this — and in fact this directly mirrors the freedom one has in choosing a Kraus representation for $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa ilang paraan ng pagpili sa mga vector $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$.\n"
"Sa pangkalahatan, magkakaroon ng maraming paraan upang gawin ito — at sa katunayan ito ay direktang sumasalamin sa kalayaan na mayroon tayo sa pagpili ng Kraus representation para sa $\\Phi$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to obtain such an expression is to first use the spectral theorem to write\n"
msgstr "Isang paraan upang makuha ang ganitong expression ay ang unang paggamit ng spectral theorem upang isulat\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in which $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $J(\\Phi)$ (which are necessarily nonnegative real numbers because $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite) and $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ are unit eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ ay ang mga eigenvalue ng $J(\\Phi)$ (na kinakailangang nonnegative real number dahil ang $J(\\Phi)$ ay positive semidefinite) at ang $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ ay unit eigenvectors na tumutugma sa mga eigenvalue na $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that, while there's no freedom in choosing the eigenvalues (except for how they're ordered), there is freedom in the choice of the eigenvectors, particularly when there are eigenvalues with multiplicity larger than one.\n"
"So, this is not a unique expression of $J(\\Phi)$ — we're just assuming we have one such expression.\n"
"Regardless, because the eigenvalues are nonnegative real numbers, they have nonnegative square roots, and so we can select\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na, bagama't walang kalayaan sa pagpili ng mga eigenvalue (maliban sa kung paano ito ina-order), mayroon namang kalayaan sa pagpili ng mga eigenvector, lalo na kapag may mga eigenvalue na may multiplicity na mas malaki sa isa.\n"
"Kaya, hindi ito natatanging expression ng $J(\\Phi)$ — ipinapalagay lang natin na mayroon tayong ganitong expression.\n"
"Gayunpaman, dahil ang mga eigenvalue ay nonnegative real number, mayroon silang nonnegative square root, kaya't maaari nating piliin ang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for each $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ to obtain an expression of the form $(1)$.\n"
msgstr "para sa bawat $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ upang makuha ang isang expression na anyong $(1)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, however, not essential that the expression $(1)$ comes from a spectral decomposition in this way, and in particular the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal in general.\n"
"It is noteworthy, though, that we can choose these vectors to be orthogonal if we wish — and moreover we never need $N$ to be larger than $nm$\n"
"(recalling that $n$ and $m$ denote the numbers of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$, respectively).\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi naman kinakailangan, gayunpaman, na ang expression $(1)$ ay nagmula sa isang spectral decomposition sa ganitong paraan, at sa partikular ang mga vector $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ ay hindi kailangang maging orthogonal sa pangkalahatan.\n"
"Kapansin-pansin, gayunpaman, na maaari nating piliin ang mga vector na ito na maging orthogonal kung nais natin — at higit pa rito hindi natin kailanman kailangang gawing mas malaki ang $N$ kaysa sa $nm$\n"
"(inaalala na ang $n$ at $m$ ay tumutukoy sa bilang ng mga classical state ng $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$, ayon sa pagkakabanggit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, each of the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ can be further decomposed as\n"
msgstr "Susunod, ang bawat isa sa mga vector na $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ ay maaaring dagdag na i-decompose bilang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the vectors $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ have entries corresponding to the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ and can be explicitly determined by the equation\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang mga vector na $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ ay may mga entries na tumutugma sa mga classical state ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ at maaaring tuwirang matukoy sa pamamagitan ng equation\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\Sigma$ and $k=0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
"Although $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ are not necessarily unit vectors, this is the same process we would use to analyze what would happen if a standard basis measurement was performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$ given a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa bawat $a\\in\\Sigma$ at $k=0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
"Bagama't ang $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ ay hindi kinakailangang unit vector, ito ang parehong proseso na gagamitin natin upang suriin kung ano ang mangyayari kung isasagawa ang standard basis measurement sa system na $\\mathsf{X}$ dahil sa isang quantum state vector ng pares na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we come to the trick that makes this part of the proof work.\n"
"We define our Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ according to the following equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"At ngayon dumating na tayo sa trick na gagawing gumana ang bahaging ito ng proof.\n"
"Dinedefine natin ang ating mga Kraus matrix na $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ ayon sa sumusunod na equation.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think about this formula purely symbolically: $\\vert a\\rangle$ effectively gets flipped around to form $\\langle a\\vert$ and moved to right-hand side, forming a matrix.\n"
"For the purposes of verifying the proof, the formula is all we need.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating isipin ang formula na ito nang puro simbolikal: ang $\\vert a\\rangle$ ay epektibong napapabaligtad upang mabuo ang $\\langle a\\vert$ at inililipat sa right-hand side, na bumubuo ng matrix.\n"
"Para sa layunin ng pagbe-verify sa proof, ang formula lamang ang kailangan natin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is, however, a simple and intuitive relationship between the vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ and the matrix $A_k$, which is that by *vectorizing* $A_k$ we get $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$.\n"
"What it means to vectorize $A_k$ is that we stack the columns on top of one another (with the leftmost column on top proceeding to the rightmost on the bottom), in order to form a vector.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits, and for some choice of $k$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon, gayunpaman, isang simple at intuitive na relasyon sa pagitan ng vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ at ng matrix $A_k$, na ang ibig sabihin ay sa pamamagitan ng *pag-vectorize* ng $A_k$ nakukuha natin ang $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$.\n"
"Ang ibig sabihin ng pag-vectorize ng $A_k$ ay pinagsasama-sama natin ang mga column nang paisa-isa sa ibabaw ng isa't isa (kung saan ang pinakakaliwang column ay nasa itaas hanggang sa pinakakanang nasa ibaba), upang bumuo ng isang vector.\n"
"Halimbawa, kung ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay parehong qubit, at para sa ilang pagpili ng $k$ mayroon tayong\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then\n"
msgstr "then\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_k & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{10}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_k & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{10}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Beware: sometimes the vectorization of a matrix is defined in a slightly different way, which is that the *rows* of the matrix are transposed and stacked on top of one another to form a column vector.)\n"
msgstr "(Mag-ingat: minsan ang vectorization ng isang matrix ay depinado sa bahagyang ibang paraan, na kung saan ang mga *row* ng matrix ay tina-transpose at pinagsasama-sama sa ibabaw ng isa't isa upang bumuo ng column vector.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll verify that this choice of Kraus matrices correctly describes the mapping $\\Phi$, after which we'll verify the other required condition.\n"
"To keep things straight, let's define a new mapping $\\Psi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una nating i-verify na ang pagpiling ito ng mga Kraus matrix ay tama ang paglalarawan sa mapping na $\\Phi$, pagkatapos nito ay i-verify natin ang iba pang kinakailangang kondisyon.\n"
"Upang manatiling malinaw, tukuyin natin ang isang bagong mapping na $\\Psi$ tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Psi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Psi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, our goal is to verify that $\\Psi = \\Phi$.\n"
msgstr "Kaya, ang ating layunin ay i-verify na ang $\\Psi = \\Phi$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way we can do this is to compare the Choi representations of these mappings.\n"
"Choi representations are faithful, so we have $\\Psi = \\Phi$ if and only if $J(\\Phi) = J(\\Psi)$.\n"
"At this point we can simply compute $J(\\Psi)$ using the expressions\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paraan na magagawa natin ito ay ihambing ang mga Choi representation ng mga mapping na ito.\n"
"Ang mga Choi representation ay faithful, kaya mayroon tayong $\\Psi = \\Phi$ kung at kung tanging kung $J(\\Phi) = J(\\Psi)$.\n"
"Sa puntong ito, maaari na lamang nating kalkulahin ang $J(\\Psi)$ gamit ang mga expression\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "together with the bilinearity of tensor products to simplify.\n"
msgstr "kasama ang bilinearity ng tensor products upang gawing simple.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Psi) & = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert A_k^{\\dagger}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1}  \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle b\\vert \\otimes \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\\biggr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = J(\\Phi)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Psi) & = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert A_k^{\\dagger}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1}  \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle b\\vert \\otimes \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\\biggr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = J(\\Phi)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, our Kraus matrices correctly describe $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nananatiling suriin ang kinakailangang kondisyon sa $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$, na lumalabas na katumbas ng pagpapalagay na $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (na hindi pa natin nagagamit).\n"
"Ipapakita natin ang relasyong ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to check the required condition on $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$, which turns out to be equivalent to the assumption $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (which we haven't used yet).\n"
"What we'll show is this relationship:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nananatiling suriin ang kinakailangang kondisyon sa $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$, na lumalabas na katumbas ng assumption na $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (na hindi pa natin nagagamit).\n"
"Ang ating ipapakita ay ang relasyon na ito:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr)^{T} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr)^{T} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(in which we're referring the *matrix transpose* on the left-hand side).\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula sa kaliwa, maaari muna tayong mapansin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting on the left, we can first observe that\n"
msgstr "Simula sa kaliwa, mapapansin muna natin na\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T\n"
"& = \\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)^T\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T\n"
"& = \\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)^T\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last equality follows from the fact that the transpose is linear and maps $\\vert b\\rangle\\langle a \\vert$ to $\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert$.\n"
msgstr "Ang huling equality ay galing sa katotohanan na ang transpose ay linear at nagma-map ng $\\vert b\\rangle\\langle a \\vert$ tungo sa $\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moving to the right-hand side of our equation, we have\n"
msgstr "Papunta sa right-hand side ng ating equation, mayroon tayong\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k \\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k \\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore\n"
msgstr "at samakatuwid\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\bigr)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\bigr)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've obtained the same result, and therefore the equation $(2)$ has been verified.\n"
"It follows, by the assumption $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, that\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakuha natin ang parehong resulta, at samakatuwid ang equation $(2)$ ay na-verify na.\n"
"Sumusunod, sa pamamagitan ng assumption na $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, na\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore, because the identity matrix is its own transpose, the required condition is true.\n"
msgstr "at samakatuwid, dahil ang identity matrix ay sarili nitong transpose, ang kinakailangang kondisyon ay totoo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Kraus to Stinespring representations {#kraus-to-stinespring-representations}"
msgstr "Mula sa Kraus patungo sa Stinespring na representasyon {#kraus-to-stinespring-representations}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now suppose that we have a Kraus representation of a mapping\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong Kraus na representasyon ng isang pagmamapa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for which\n"
msgstr "kung saan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to find a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr "Ang ating layunin ay hanapin ang Stinespring representation para sa $\\Phi$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What we'd like to do first is to choose the garbage system $\\mathsf{G}$ so that its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"For $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ to have the same size, however, it must be that\n"
"$n$ divides $m N$, allowing us to take $\\mathsf{W}$ to have classical states $\\{0,\\ldots,d-1\\}$ for $d = mN/n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang arbitrary na pagpili ng $n$, $m$, at $N$, maaaring hindi integer ang $mN/n$, kaya hindi tayo talaga malaya na piliin ang $\\mathsf{G}$ upang ang klasikal na set ng estado nito ay $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"Ngunit maaari nating palaging dagdagan ang $N$ nang arbitraryo sa Kraus na representasyon sa pamamagitan ng pagpili ng $A_k = 0$ para sa kung gaano karaming karagdagang halaga ng $k$ ang nais natin.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an arbitrary choice of $n$, $m$, and $N$, it may not be the case that $mN/n$ is an integer, so we're not actually free to choose $\\mathsf{G}$ so that it's classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"But we can always increase $N$ arbitrarily in the Kraus representation by choosing $A_k = 0$ for however many additional values of $k$ that we wish.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, kung ipapalagay nating ang $mN/n$ ay isang integer, na katumbas ng pagiging multiple ng $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m)$ ng $N,$ malaya tayong kunin ang $\\mathsf{G}$ upang ang klasikal na set ng estado nito ay $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Lalo na, kung ang $N = nm,$ maaari tayong kunin ang $\\mathsf{W}$ na may $m^2$ na mga klasikal na estado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we tacitly assume that $mN/n$ is an integer, which is equivalent to $N$ being a multiple of $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m)$, then we're free to take $\\mathsf{G}$ so that its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"In particular, if it is the case that $N = nm$, then we may take $\\mathsf{W}$ to have $m^2$ classical states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, kung tahasan nating ipagpalagay na ang $mN/n$ ay isang integer, na katumbas ng $N$ na multiple ng $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m)$, kung gayon malaya tayong kunin ang $\\mathsf{G}$ upang ang classical state set nito ay $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"Sa partikular, kung ang kaso ay $N = nm$, maaari nating kunin ang $\\mathsf{W}$ upang magkaroon ng $m^2$ classical state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It remains to choose $U$, and we'll do this by matching the following pattern.\n"
msgstr "Nananatiling piliin ang $U$, at gagawin natin ito sa pamamagitan ng pagtutugma sa sumusunod na pattern.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, this pattern is meant to suggest a block matrix, where each block (including $A_{0},\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ as well as the blocks marked with a question mark) has $m$ rows and $n$ columns.\n"
"There are $N$ rows of blocks, which means that there are $d = mN/n$ columns of blocks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang maging malinaw, ang pattern na ito ay ipinahihiwatig upang magmungkahi ng block matrix, kung saan ang bawat block (kasama ang $A_{0},\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ pati na rin ang mga block na markado ng question mark) ay may $m$ row at $n$ column.\n"
"Mayroong $N$ row ng mga block, na nangangahulugang mayroong $d = mN/n$ column ng mga block.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed in more formulaic terms, we will define $U$ as\n"
msgstr "Sa mas formulaic na termino, i-definite natin ang $U$ bilang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U & = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle j \\vert \\otimes M_{k,j} \\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} & \\cdots & M_{0,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1} & \\cdots & M_{1,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{N-1,0} & M_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & M_{N-1,d-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U & = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle j \\vert \\otimes M_{k,j} \\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} & \\cdots & M_{0,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1} & \\cdots & M_{1,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{N-1,0} & M_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & M_{N-1,d-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where each matrix $M_{k,j}$ has $m$ rows and $n$ columns, and in particular we shall take $M_{k,0} = A_k$ for $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang bawat matrix na $M_{k,j}$ ay may $m$ row at $n$ column, at sa partikular kukunin natin ang $M_{k,0} = A_k$ para sa $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This must be a unitary matrix, and the blocks labeled with a question mark, or equivalently $M_{k,j}$ for $j>0$, must be selected with this in mind — but aside from allowing $U$ to be unitary, the blocks labeled with a question mark won't have any relevance to the proof.\n"
msgstr "Kailangan itong maging unitary matrix, at ang mga block na markado ng question mark, o katumbas na $M_{k,j}$ para sa $j>0$, ay dapat piliin nang may isip ito — ngunit maliban sa pagpapahintulot sa $U$ na maging unitary, ang mga block na markado ng question mark ay walang kaugnayan sa proof.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's momentarily disregard the concern that $U$ is unitary and focus on the expression\n"
msgstr "Kalimutan muna natin sandali ang alalahanin na ang $U$ ay unitary at magtuon sa expression\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that describes the output state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ given the input state $\\rho$ of $\\mathsf{X}$ for our Stinespring representation.\n"
"We can alternatively write\n"
msgstr ""
"na naglalarawan ng output state ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ dahil sa input state $\\rho$ ng $\\mathsf{X}$ para sa ating Stinespring representation.\n"
"Maaari nating alternatibong isulat\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) \\rho (\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) U^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) \\rho (\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) U^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and we see from our choice of $U$ that\n"
msgstr "at makikita natin mula sa ating pagpili ng $U$ na\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We therefore find that\n"
msgstr "Kaya't makikita natin na\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert \\otimes A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert \\otimes A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and so\n"
msgstr "and so\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"& = \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert\\bigr) \\, A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\Phi(\\rho).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"& = \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert\\bigr) \\, A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\Phi(\\rho).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We therefore have a correct representation for the mapping $\\Phi$, and it remains to verify that we can choose $U$ to be unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang unang $n$ na mga kolumna ng $U$ kapag ito ay pinili ayon sa pattern sa itaas.\n"
"Kinukuha ang mga kolumnang ito lamang, mayroon tayong isang block matrix\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the first $n$ columns of $U$ when it's selected according to the pattern above.\n"
"Taking these columns alone, we have a block matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang unang $n$ column ng $U$ kapag ito ay pinili ayon sa pattern sa itaas.\n"
"Kung kukunin lamang ang mga column na ito, mayroon tayong block matrix\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are $n$ columns, one for each classical state of $\\mathsf{X}$, and as vectors let us name the columns as $\\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Here's a formula for these vectors that can be matched to the block matrix representation above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroong $n$ column, isa para sa bawat classical state ng $\\mathsf{X}$, at bilang mga vector tawagin natin ang mga column bilang $\\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle$ para sa bawat $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Narito ang isang formula para sa mga vector na ito na maaaring itugma sa block matrix representation sa itaas.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\gamma_a\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\gamma_a\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's compute the inner product between any two of these vectors, meaning the ones corresponding to any choice of $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, kalkulahin natin ang inner product sa pagitan ng anumang dalawa sa mga vector na ito, ibig sabihin ang mga tumutugma sa anumang pagpili ng $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle k \\vert j \\rangle \\, \\langle a \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} A_j \\vert b\\rangle =\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr) \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle k \\vert j \\rangle \\, \\langle a \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} A_j \\vert b\\rangle =\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr) \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By the assumption\n"
msgstr "Sa pamamagitan ng assumption\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "we conclude that the $n$ column vectors $\\{\\vert\\gamma_a\\rangle\\,:\\,a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ form an orthonormal set:\n"
msgstr "napagpapasyahan natin na ang $n$ column vector na $\\{\\vert\\gamma_a\\rangle\\,:\\,a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ ay bumubuo ng orthonormal set:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & a = b\\\\\n"
"0 & a\\neq b\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & a = b\\\\\n"
"0 & a\\neq b\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay nagpapahiwatig na posible ang pagpuno ng natitirang mga kolumna ng $U$ upang ito ay maging isang unitary matrix.\n"
"Lalo na, ang proseso ng Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization ay maaaring gamitin upang piliin ang natitirang mga kolumna.\n"
"Isang bagay na katulad nito ang ginawa sa leksyon ng *Quantum circuits* ng \"Basics of quantum information\" sa konteksto ng problemang state discrimination.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that it is possible to fill out the remaining columns of $U$ so that it becomes a unitary matrix.\n"
"In particular, the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process can be used to select the remaining columns.\n"
"Something similar was done in the *Quantum circuits* lesson of \"Basics of quantum information\" in the context of the state discrimination problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapahiwatig nito na posibleng punuin ang natitirang mga column ng $U$ upang ito ay maging unitary matrix.\n"
"Sa partikular, ang Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process ay maaaring gamitin upang piliin ang natitirang mga column.\n"
"May katulad na ginawa sa *Quantum circuits* lesson ng \"Basics of quantum information\" sa konteksto ng state discrimination problem.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stinespring representations back to the definition {#stinespring-representations-back-to-the-definition}"
msgstr "Mula sa Stinespring na representasyon pabalik sa kahulugan {#stinespring-representations-back-to-the-definition}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The final implication is 4 $\\Rightarrow$ 1.\n"
"That is, we assume that we have a unitary operation transforming a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ into a pair\n"
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, and our goal is to conclude that the mapping\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling implikasyon ay 4 $\\Rightarrow$ 1.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, ipinapalagay natin na mayroon tayong isang unitary na operasyon na nagtatransporma ng isang pares ng mga sistema $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ patungo sa isang pares\n"
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, at ang ating layunin ay masabing ang pagmamapa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a valid channel.\n"
"From its form, it is evident that $\\Phi$ is linear, and it remains to verify that it always transforms density matrices into density matrices.\n"
"This is pretty straightforward and we've already discussed the key points.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay isang wastong channel.\n"
"Mula sa anyo nito, malinaw na ang $\\Phi$ ay linear, at nananatili na i-verify na lagi nitong tinatransporma ang mga density matrix patungo sa mga density matrix.\n"
"Ito ay medyo diretso at napag-usapan na natin ang mga pangunahing punto.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, if we start with a density matrix $\\sigma$ of a compound system $(\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$, and then add on an additional workspace system $\\mathsf{W}$, we will certainly be left with a density matrix.\n"
"If we reorder the systems $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$ for convenience, we can write this state as\n"
msgstr ""
"Lalo na, kung magsimula tayo sa isang density matrix na $\\sigma$ ng isang compound na sistema $(\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$, at pagkatapos ay magdagdag ng karagdagang workspace system na $\\mathsf{W}$, tiyak na maiiwan tayo ng isang density matrix.\n"
"Kung muling iayos natin ang mga sistema $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$ para sa kaginhawaan, maaari tayong isulat ang estado na ito bilang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then apply the unitary operation $U$, and as we already discussed this is a valid channel, and hence maps density matrices to density matrices.\n"
"Finally, the partial trace of a density matrix is another density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilalapat natin ang unitary na operasyon na $U$, at tulad ng napag-usapan na natin ito ay isang wastong channel, at kaya nagmamapa ng mga density matrix patungo sa mga density matrix.\n"
"Sa wakas, ang partial trace ng isang density matrix ay isa pang density matrix.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another way to say this is to observe first that each of these things is a valid channel:\n"
msgstr "Isa pang paraan upang sabihin ito ay ang unang pagmamasid na ang bawat isa sa mga bagay na ito ay isang wastong channel:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing an initialized workspace system.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapakilala ng isang initialized workspace system.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performing a unitary operation.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagsasagawa ng isang unitary na operasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tracing out a system.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-trace out ng isang sistema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "And finally, any composition of channels is another channel — which is immediate from the definition, but is also a fact worth observing in its own right.\n"
msgstr "At sa wakas, ang anumang komposisyon ng mga channel ay isa pang channel — na agarang sumusunod mula sa kahulugan, ngunit isa ring katotohanang kapaki-pakinabang na mapansin sa sarili nito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This completes the proof of the final implication, and therefore we've established the equivalence of the four statements listed at the start of the section.\n"
msgstr "Tinapos nito ang patunay ng huling implikasyon, at kaya naitatag na natin ang pagkakatumbas ng apat na pahayag na nakalista sa simula ng seksyon.\n"
